This directory stores translations of MLflow UI messages.

English (`en`) is the default locale. It has no runtime catalog: react-intl renders the `defaultMessage` written next to each string. `default/en.json` is the extracted source catalog used to check that those strings stay in sync (`yarn i18n` / `yarn i18n:check`).

Other locales live here as `{ id: { defaultMessage, description } }`. Message ids are the first 6 characters of the base64 SHA-512 of `defaultMessage#description`, matching babel-plugin-formatjs `idInterpolationPattern: '[sha512:contenthash:base64:6]'`.

The web UI loads `zh-CN` from `zh-CN.json`. Strings that are not in that synced catalog yet are filled from `zh-CN.supplement.json`, which `yarn i18n:zh` generates from:

1. Exact English `defaultMessage` keys in `scripts/zh-cn-overrides.js` and `scripts/zh-cn-extra-*.json` (edit these to add a translation).
2. An existing Chinese translation of the same English text, when one is already in `zh-CN.json`.

Every current English catalog id has a Chinese string. Visible labels, buttons, placeholders, and accessible names on the main screens are wrapped in react-intl. Product names (MLflow, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google Gemini, MCP), URLs, example paths and identifiers, SQL keywords such as WHERE, protocol names (Git, OCI, ZIP), and chart-axis test ids such as `x-axis-min` stay in their original form. A few older compare-chart titles (Parameters, Metrics, Plot chart, Parallel Coordinates), skeleton labels (`Loading...`), model-registry alias titles, and notebook-renderer link titles are still hardcoded English.

Missing keys fall back to the English `defaultMessage`. The language switcher (sidebar and Settings > General) stores the choice in `localStorage` under `locale` and reloads the page. With no stored choice, a Chinese browser language selects `zh-CN`; every other browser language stays on English. `?l=zh-CN` still selects a locale and saves it.

To translate a new string:

1. Wrap it in `<FormattedMessage defaultMessage="..." description="..." />` (or `intl.formatMessage`).
2. Run `yarn i18n` so `default/en.json` picks up the id.
3. Add the exact English `defaultMessage` to `scripts/zh-cn-overrides.js` or `scripts/zh-cn-extra-*.json`.
4. Run `yarn i18n:zh`.
